==============================================================================
ATTACK DETECTION QUERIES
==============================================================================
Each query is mapped to a specific MITRE ATT&CK technique.
Save these as Splunk Alerts to trigger automatically.
==============================================================================


==============================================================================
DETECTION 1: System Information Discovery
MITRE ATT&CK: T1082
==============================================================================
Attackers run systeminfo, hostname, whoami after gaining initial access to
fingerprint the system. Legitimate too — alert thresholds matter.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=1
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='User'>(?<User>[^<]+)</Data>"
| search Image="*systeminfo.exe" OR Image="*hostname.exe" OR Image="*whoami.exe" 
      OR Image="*ipconfig.exe" OR Image="*net.exe"
| table _time, User, Image, CommandLine
| sort -_time


==============================================================================
DETECTION 2: Encoded PowerShell Execution
MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001
==============================================================================
Encoded PowerShell is a heavy malware indicator. Legitimate use is rare.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=1
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ParentImage'>(?<ParentImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='User'>(?<User>[^<]+)</Data>"
| search CommandLine="*-EncodedCommand*" OR CommandLine="*-enc *" 
      OR CommandLine="*FromBase64String*"
| table _time, User, ParentImage, CommandLine
| sort -_time


==============================================================================
DETECTION 3: Brute Force Authentication (Windows Logon Failures)
MITRE ATT&CK: T1110
==============================================================================
Detects 10+ failed logons within 5 minutes from one source IP / username.

index=endpoint source="WinEventLog:Security"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=4625
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TargetUserName'>(?<TargetUserName>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='IpAddress'>(?<IpAddress>[^<]+)</Data>"
| bucket _time span=5m
| stats count by TargetUserName, IpAddress, _time
| where count > 10
| sort -count


==============================================================================
DETECTION 4: Local Admin Account Creation
MITRE ATT&CK: T1136.001
==============================================================================
Attacker creating new user/admin accounts for persistence.

index=endpoint source="WinEventLog:Security"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=4720 OR EventID=4728 OR EventID=4732
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TargetUserName'>(?<TargetUserName>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='SubjectUserName'>(?<SubjectUserName>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, EventID, SubjectUserName, TargetUserName


==============================================================================
DETECTION 5: LSASS Memory Access (Credential Dumping)
MITRE ATT&CK: T1003.001
==============================================================================
Mimikatz, Pypykatz, and similar tools access LSASS memory.
GrantedAccess 0x1010, 0x1410, 0x147a are common Mimikatz signatures.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=10
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='SourceImage'>(?<SourceImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TargetImage'>(?<TargetImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='GrantedAccess'>(?<GrantedAccess>[^<]+)</Data>"
| search TargetImage="*lsass.exe"
| search GrantedAccess IN ("0x1010", "0x1410", "0x147a", "0x1438", "0x143a")
| table _time, SourceImage, TargetImage, GrantedAccess


==============================================================================
DETECTION 6: Scheduled Task Creation
MITRE ATT&CK: T1053.005
==============================================================================
Common persistence technique.

index=endpoint source="WinEventLog:Security"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=4698
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='SubjectUserName'>(?<User>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TaskName'>(?<TaskName>[^<]+)</Data>"
| table _time, User, TaskName


==============================================================================
DETECTION 7: Suspicious Parent-Child Process (Office spawning shell)
MITRE ATT&CK: T1566.001
==============================================================================
Word/Excel spawning cmd.exe or powershell.exe = phishing payload executed.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=1
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='ParentImage'>(?<ParentImage>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| search (ParentImage="*winword.exe" OR ParentImage="*excel.exe" OR ParentImage="*outlook.exe")
      (Image="*cmd.exe" OR Image="*powershell.exe" OR Image="*wscript.exe")
| table _time, ParentImage, Image, CommandLine


==============================================================================
DETECTION 8: PowerShell Download Cradle
MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001 / T1105
==============================================================================
Catches Invoke-WebRequest, DownloadString, and similar fetch patterns.

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=1
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| search CommandLine="*Invoke-WebRequest*" OR CommandLine="*IWR *"
      OR CommandLine="*DownloadString*" OR CommandLine="*DownloadFile*"
      OR CommandLine="*Net.WebClient*" OR CommandLine="*Start-BitsTransfer*"
| table _time, User, CommandLine


==============================================================================
DETECTION 9: Successful Logon After Brute Force
MITRE ATT&CK: T1110 (chained)
==============================================================================
A successful logon (4624) on an account that recently had many failures (4625).
This indicates the attacker likely guessed the password.

index=endpoint source="WinEventLog:Security"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='TargetUserName'>(?<TargetUserName>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='IpAddress'>(?<IpAddress>[^<]+)</Data>"
| eval result = if(EventID=4625, "fail", if(EventID=4624, "success", null()))
| stats values(result) as results count(eval(result="fail")) as fails 
        count(eval(result="success")) as success
        by TargetUserName, IpAddress
| where fails > 5 AND success > 0


==============================================================================
DETECTION 10: Living-Off-the-Land Binaries (LOLBins)
MITRE ATT&CK: Various
==============================================================================
Catches abuse of legitimate Windows binaries (LOLBins).

index=endpoint sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
| rex field=_raw "<EventID>(?<EventID>\d+)</EventID>"
| search EventID=1
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='Image'>(?<Image>[^<]+)</Data>"
| rex field=_raw "<Data Name='CommandLine'>(?<CommandLine>[^<]+)</Data>"
| search Image IN ("*certutil.exe", "*bitsadmin.exe", "*mshta.exe", 
                   "*regsvr32.exe", "*rundll32.exe", "*wmic.exe", 
                   "*installutil.exe", "*msbuild.exe")
| table _time, Image, CommandLine, User
| sort -_time
